JST>2026-11-04T22:40:00.948604+09:00</chr2:firstObservedAtJST><pubDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 13:15:04 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>Godot のゲームに AI で効果音を入れる方法（ElevenLabs・sfxr などとの比較つき）</title><link>https://zenn.dev/zivaengine/articles/512c0785718b9d</link><guid isPermaLink="false">urn:sha256:70da9b9f1e863ca1d75f78893ca428fc1688dd06d6bce6a14f4757f3cb67e7b3</guid><category>ZENN</category><chr2:sourceName>Zenn</chr2:sourceName><chr2:firstObservedAtJST>2026-11-04T22:40:00.948604+09:00</chr2:firstObservedAtJST><pubDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 12:46:30 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title>The Classics Return: Vulnerable E-Mail Scripts, (Wed, Nov 4th)</title><link>https://isc.sans.edu/diary/33488</link><guid isPermaLink="false">urn:sha256:b7de05e5dabf990dead022d8640b32c99d1a68e5883d39d64705cdb1dbf17517</guid><category>NEWS</category><chr2:sourceName>SANS Internet Storm Center</chr2:sourceName><chr2:firstObservedAtJST>2026-11-04T22:27:24.140582+09:00</chr2:firstObservedAtJST><pubDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 13:24:13 GMT</pubDate><description>One of the early web application vulnerabilities I remember was CVE-2000-0411 [CVE]. This was a simple vulnerability in a CGI-bin script used to send e-mail. The vulnerability was pretty straightforward: Adding additional parameters to the URL leaked environment variables. Other vulnerabilities allowed setting the "To" address and were heavily abused by spammers. And if parameters were passed directly to the sendmail binary, similar vulnerabilities could allow arbitrary code execution.</description><chr2:heatScore>55.0</chr2:heatScore></item><item><title>French blood service hit by cyber attack threatening to turn stocks into “black pudding”</title><link>https://www.itpro.com/security/cyber-attacks/french-blood-service-hit-by-new-cyber-attack-threatening-to-turn-stocks-into-black-pudding</link><guid isPermaLink="false">urn:sha256:96574d6ab9315734f27c557fda89925ce64ea50a7e9f2393c3cc2f3e1b4727d5</guid><category>NEWS</category><chr2:sourceName>ITPro Security</chr2:sourceName><chr2:firstObservedAtJST>2026-11-04T22:27:16.453002+09:00</chr2:firstObservedAtJST><pubDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 12:10:59 GMT</pubDate><description>The attack on cold rooms at Coolworld happened the same night as attacks on fridges in Benelux and Sweden</description><chr2:heatScore>65.0</chr2:heatScore></item><item><title>Phishing-Resistant Isn't Enough; Yubico Takes Aim at Identity-Verification Gap</title><link>https://www.darkreading.com/identity-access-management-security/beyond-phishing-resistant-yubico-identity-verification-gap</link><guid isPermaLink="false">urn:sha256:c8e5e05cfbad0528784ce99fb788dffa7afe3438a66a447de7a2c0397eeb3d46</guid><category>NEWS</category><chr2:sourceName>Dark Reading</chr2:sourceName><chr2:firstObservedAtJST>2026-11-04T22:27:09.492256+09:00</chr2:firstObservedAtJST><pubDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 01:05:40 GMT</pubDate><description>The new YubiID service bridges identity verification with credential enrollment and recovery across existing identity platforms, closing a phishing-resistant authentication gap. Plus: post-quantum YubiKey beta.</description><chr2:heatScore>58.5</chr2:heatScore></item></channel></rss>